        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Constantine the Great</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 272 CE – 337 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">27 February 272 (the year is not recorded; scholars have proposed 271 to 280) at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nis">Naissus</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a> Superior, now Niš in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>; son of the army officer Flavius Constantius, later one of the four emperors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetrarchy">Tetrarchy</a>, and of Helena, a Greek woman of low social standing</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">22 May 337 at the suburban villa of Achyron near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicomedia">Nicomedia</a>, of an illness that began after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter">Easter</a>, having been baptised on his deathbed by Eusebius of Nicomedia</span></div>
